@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@cindex introduction
@cindex transcript-parser skill

latex-parser-skill turns raw dictated or transcribed text in a @LaTeX{} buffer into a structured @LaTeX{} fragment.
The fragment has one @samp{\subsubsection} per topic, @samp{\index} keys below each heading, one sentence per line, expanded contractions, and a closing checklist of TODO items.
The rules come from the transcript-parser skill, and a copy of its instructions ships with the package.

The package is meant for text that did not pass through a dictation tool with its own clean-up step.
That text still holds contractions and dictation errors, so the package fixes the predictable ones before the model sees it.

An analogy from crystallography describes the four stages.
Stage 1 is like data reduction because it is deterministic and repeatable.
Stage 2 is like model building because it needs judgment.
Stage 3 is like validation because it checks the model against fixed rules.
Stage 4 is like a short round of rebuilding guided by the validation report.

@float Table,org7b87a5e
@multitable {aaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Stage
@tab Name
@tab Kind
@tab What it does
@item 1
@tab Replacements
@tab Deterministic
@tab Expands contractions and applies your dictation rule files
@item 2
@tab Parse
@tab Model
@tab Sends the skill instructions and the text to the backend
@item 3
@tab Verify
@tab Deterministic
@tab Checks the reply against the rules of the skill
@item 4
@tab Repair
@tab Model
@tab Sends the list of violations back for a corrective pass
@end multitable
@caption{The four stages of the pipeline.}
@end float

@node Installation
@chapter Installation

@cindex installation
@cindex MELPA

The package needs Emacs 28.1 or later.
Install it from MELPA with @samp{M-x package-install RET latex-parser-skill RET}.

To install from the repository with Emacs 29 or later, use the @samp{:vc} keyword of @samp{use-package}.

@lisp
(use-package latex-parser-skill
  :vc (:url "https://github.com/MooersLab/latex-parser-skill-el" :rev :newest))
@end lisp

A manual install needs only the repository on the @samp{load-path}.

@lisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "~/6112MooersLabGitHubLabRepos/latex-parser-skill-el")
(require 'latex-parser-skill)
@end lisp

See the chapter on key bindings for the suggested @samp{C-c t} prefix.

@node Backends
@chapter Backends

@cindex backends

A backend sends the system prompt and one user message to a model and returns the reply.
Every backend is asynchronous, so Emacs stays responsive.
Choose the default with @samp{latex-parser-skill-backend} and switch for the session with @samp{C-c t m}.

