@node Claude Code
@section Claude Code

@cindex claude-code backend

This is the default backend.
It runs @samp{claude -p} with the transcript on standard input.
The bundled prompt replaces the system prompt, and every tool is turned off with @samp{--tools ""}, so the model only writes text.
Sessions are not saved, because the command passes @samp{--no-session-persistence}.

@lisp
(setq latex-parser-skill-claude-model "sonnet")   ; nil uses the program default
@end lisp

Set @samp{latex-parser-skill-claude-prompt-source} to @samp{skill} to rely on a transcript-parser skill installed in Claude Code instead of the bundled prompt.
Extra command-line arguments go in @samp{latex-parser-skill-claude-extra-args}.

@node Claude API
@section Claude API

@cindex anthropic-api backend
@cindex auth-source

The key comes from auth-source under the host @samp{api.anthropic.com}, or from the environment variable @samp{ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}.
A line in @samp{~/.authinfo.gpg} looks like this.

@example
machine api.anthropic.com password sk-ant-...
@end example

The model is @samp{latex-parser-skill-anthropic-model}.

@node Local models
@section Local models

@cindex openai-compatible backend
@cindex Ollama
@cindex llama.cpp

Any server that speaks the chat completions protocol works, including Ollama, the llama.cpp server, LM Studio and vLLM@.
The default URL is the Ollama server on this computer.

@lisp
(setq latex-parser-skill-openai-url "http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions"
      latex-parser-skill-openai-model "your-model-tag")
@end lisp

A server that needs a key reads it from auth-source under the host of the URL@.
Requests set the temperature to zero.
Replies from reasoning models often begin with a @samp{<think>} block, which the package removes.

Local models have smaller context windows.
@samp{latex-parser-skill-chunk-sizes} splits long input at blank lines for named backends, and its default limits @samp{openai-compatible} to 12000 characters per request.
The trade-off is that a topic that spans two chunks may get two headings.
The merge step collects every TODO item into one block at the end.

@node gptel
@section gptel

@cindex gptel backend

The gptel backend reuses the model that gptel already knows about.
It uses @samp{gptel-backend} and @samp{gptel-model} unless @samp{latex-parser-skill-gptel-backend} or @samp{latex-parser-skill-gptel-model} say otherwise.
gptel is optional, and the package loads it only when this backend runs.
Set @samp{latex-parser-skill-gptel-remote} to nil when gptel talks to a local server, so that no confirmation is asked.

@node Writing a new backend
@section Writing a new backend

@cindex custom backend

Register a function of four arguments.
It receives the system prompt, the user message, a success callback and an error callback, and it returns a handle.

@lisp
(latex-parser-skill-register-backend
 'my-backend
 :request (lambda (system text callback errback)
            (my-send system text callback errback))
 :remote t
 :cancel (lambda (handle) (my-abort handle))
 :description "My model server")
@end lisp

The default cancel function kills a process or a buffer, so many backends do not need @samp{:cancel}.

@node Stage 1 replacements
@chapter Stage 1 replacements

@cindex Stage 1
@cindex contractions
@cindex rule files

Stage 1 is self-contained and needs no other package.
It reads the bundled contraction table, then each file in @samp{latex-parser-skill-replacement-files}, then @samp{latex-parser-skill-replacement-alist}.
A later source overrides an earlier one for the same trigger.

A rule file is a CSV file of @samp{trigger,replacement} lines.
Lines that start with @samp{#} are comments, and a header line is skipped.
Triggers may hold several words.
Matching ignores case, respects word boundaries, skips @LaTeX{} commands and comments, and keeps the case of the original.

Contractions that end in @samp{'s} or @samp{'d} have two readings, such as "it's" for "it is" or "it has".
By default Stage 1 leaves them for the model, which reads the whole sentence.
Set @samp{latex-parser-skill-skip-ambiguous} to nil to expand them with the first reading.

Triggers listed in @samp{latex-parser-skill-replacement-deny} never fire.
Set @samp{latex-parser-skill-run-replacements} to nil to skip the stage.

An external program can replace the built-in engine.
The string @samp{%f} in an argument becomes the name of a temporary file that holds the text, and the program prints the result.

@lisp
(setq latex-parser-skill-replacement-command
      '("python3" "/path/to/apply_replacements.py" "%f" "--skip-ambiguous" "-o" "-"))
@end lisp

@node Verification rules
@chapter Verification rules

@cindex verification
@cindex violations

Stage 3 mirrors the Verification section of the skill.
Errors trigger the repair pass, and warnings only appear in the report.

@float Table,orgf46b480
@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Check
@tab Level
@tab Rule
@item @samp{preamble}
@tab Error
@tab No @samp{\documentclass}, @samp{\usepackage} or document environment lines
@item @samp{index}
@tab Error
@tab Every @samp{\subsubsection} is followed by an @samp{\index} line
@item @samp{contraction}
@tab Error
@tab No contraction from the table remains, and possessives are fine
@item @samp{sound}
@tab Error
@tab No sound description such as @samp{(coughing)} remains
@item @samp{todo}
@tab Error
@tab The TODO block is closed and comes last
@item @samp{todo}
@tab Warning
@tab No TODO block was found
@item @samp{dash}
@tab Error
@tab No em-dash or triple hyphen appears
@item @samp{one-sentence}
@tab Warning
@tab A line may hold two sentences
@end multitable
@caption{Checks run by Stage 3.}
@end float

Choose the checks with @samp{latex-parser-skill-verify-checks} and extend the sound list with @samp{latex-parser-skill-sound-descriptions}.
The repair pass runs for every backend.
@samp{latex-parser-skill-repair-attempts} sets how many passes each chunk may get, and zero turns the stage off.

